{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_18a6cd4de6fa879994156b1c5cf0f3bcdadf0b05d43839939447cebffb9cabfb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The ACE Step 1.5 audio tool exposes admin valves for workflow node IDs and per-user valves for steps, seed, and audio-code generation, supporting batch generation and an embedded player."},{"claim_ids":["clm_332b55692b608edfef1bf021b3e04f32a6a132357a31565facf30ab37f392cf2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The ComfyUI image-editing tool supports three workflow types (Qwen Edit 2509 default, Flux Kontext, or custom JSON), with Qwen accepting 1-3 input images and Flux Kontext currently single-image."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5b9db23ee25da91a003f6c302ecc6df557d8c7e0ff26ccb4876e5898c4a8296e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The arXiv Search tool requires no API key and no configuration, returning up to five recent papers per query."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8606e56d0e05323801b4a184e682ecd063f887535e553568aa1198d204ca2973"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Function pipes include Planner Agent v3, arXiv Research MCTS, Multi Model Conversations v2, Resume Analyzer, Mopidy Music Controller, Letta Agent, Perplexica Pipe, Google Veo, and MiniMax LLM Pipe."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8a64ecd9afe1fdfb3a45699cc247ee3e87534f24bf07a490858505f38e28b53d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Installation is either via the Open WebUI Hub page or manually by copying .py files from tools/, functions/, or filters/ into the Open WebUI Workspace."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9105553d505be45d3c217b908b94f131a74fb8059212773434a65df69b3ce7cf"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Several tools require external services or keys: a self-hosted Perplexica instance with Ollama models, a Pexels API key, a YouTube Data API v3 key, and a running ComfyUI for media generation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_998ef8f72884f9c30861e81eeb3425441896c1fc524897ac81942661e25019d5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Filters include Doodle Paint, Prompt Enhancer, Semantic Router, Full Document, Clean Thinking Tags, and OpenRouter WebSearch Citations."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9a26dc7dd1b8c2d9929b49f9b9065634d76c3016fd8c1e58a179fc250e7c60de"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repository advertises 20+ specialized tools and functions organized as tools, function pipes, and filters for Open WebUI."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a6e547b7ce803a875438302ea1b5c7c67404bdbc29a01599e46c92a149a99959"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The Pexels tool exposes three search functions (search_photos, search_videos, get_curated_photos) and caps results per page to avoid overwhelming LLMs."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b14067a7dd581fe01c673614a1d6128609800277b5d17bf7cfa90c130118b8fd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Tools include arXiv Search, Perplexica Search, Pexels Media Search, YouTube Search & Embed, multiple ComfyUI-based image/audio/video generators, and an OpenWeatherMap forecast tool."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d1aec58e9d240fb773763bf063e6b3f10fcd5d527dcf08fe4140ab7c285937da"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The Perplexica Pipe streams responses, emits citations with source metadata, supports multiple focus modes, and routes between search and non-search task models."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d4da6b2fd9ac3976edd9887cd0a23f8710335098605fea808424eb88eff35dca"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Tools are configured through Open WebUI Valves settings; for example the YouTube tool exposes YOUTUBE_API_KEY, MAX_RESULTS, REGION_CODE, and SAFE_SEARCH valves."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ee43eebb3276d7db0556fd829db4dd39eabd727ab20f79d9b868d28c15697514"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The Native Image Generator is backend-agnostic, using whatever image backend is configured in Open WebUI admin settings, with optional Ollama model unloading to free VRAM."}],"claim_ids":["clm_18a6cd4de6fa879994156b1c5cf0f3bcdadf0b05d43839939447cebffb9cabfb","clm_332b55692b608edfef1bf021b3e04f32a6a132357a31565facf30ab37f392cf2","clm_5b9db23ee25da91a003f6c302ecc6df557d8c7e0ff26ccb4876e5898c4a8296e","clm_8606e56d0e05323801b4a184e682ecd063f88